  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(6, 4, 8)\n\n(17, 6, 28)\n\n**Logic:** First no. = [(Second no. + Third no.) ÷ 2]\n\n**(6, 4, 8) →**\n\n⇒ [(4 + 8) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (12 ÷ 2) = 6\n\n**(17, 6, 28) →**\n\n⇒ [(6 + 28) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (34 ÷ 2) = 17\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (8, 3, 12)\n\n⇒ [(12 + 3) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (15 ÷ 2) = 7.5\n\n**2. **(12, 9, 11)\n\n⇒ [(9 + 11) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (20 ÷ 2) = 10\n\n**3. **(11, 4, 19)\n\n⇒ [(19 + 4) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (23 ÷ 2) = 11.5\n\n**4. ****(13, 5, 21)**\n\n⇒ [(5 + 21) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (26 ÷ 2) = **13**\n\nHere, **(13, 5, 21)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (4)\".",
